[h1]Languages[/h1][url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/who-i-am/README/README.html]EN/English[/url] | [url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/who-i-am/README/README_ZH-CN.html]ZH-CN/简体中文[/url]
[h1]Who I Am[/h1]A client-side Fabric mod that displays your own Minecraft player name in places where it is normally hidden.
This mod runs entirely on the client and does [b]not[/b] modify any server behavior.
[h2]Features[/h2][list]
[*]Shows your own name tag in third-person view[/*]
[*]Shows your own name tag when the camera is detached from the local player, including free-camera views[/*]
[*]Appends the current player name to the end of the Minecraft window title[/*]
[*]Provides the client-side [b]/i[/b] command to display the current player name[/*]
[*]No server-side plugin or mod required[/*]
[/list][h2]Commands[/h2][h3]Show current player name[/h3][code]/i[/code]
[list]
[*]Prints [b]You are: <player name>[/b] in the client chat[/*]
[*]The command is handled locally and is not sent to the server[/*]
[/list][h2]How It Works[/h2][list]
[*]The mod reads the current player name from the active Minecraft client session[/*]
[*]When the local player model is rendered:
[list]
[*]The name tag is forced to display in third-person view[/*]
[*]The name tag is also forced to display when the camera is detached from the local player[/*]
[/list][/*]
[*]Whenever Minecraft generates the window title, the player name is appended to the end[/*]
[*]Running [b]/i[/b] displays the same player name in the client chat[/*]
[/list]The mod does [b]not[/b] send additional packets, require server support, or modify server-side player data.
[h2]Supported Versions[/h2][list]
[*]Minecraft 26.1.2[/*]
[*]Fabric Loader 0.19.2+[/*]
[*]Fabric API 0.150.0+[/*]
[*]Java 25[/*]
[/list][h2]License[/h2]MIT
